DTSTAMP:20261031T115744Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261014
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261015
SUMMARY:Deadline: ANAT: Synapse Residency Program 2027 (Australia)
DESCRIPTION:ANAT's flagship Synapse program embeds an Australian artist in 
 an Australian research organisation for 16 weeks of self-guided creative r
 esearch with no required outcome\; one residency is on offer in 2027. The 
 artist identifies their own host and submits a joint application led by th
 e artist\, so hosts can span any science or technology field\, from medica
 l research institutes and digital health labs to engineering and environme
 ntal science\; Synapse has a long history of art-science pairings across d
 isciplines. WHAT YOU GET: a total artist fee of AUD 19\,250 ex GST plus 12
 % superannuation\, and up to AUD 3\,500 toward other project expenses. ELI
 GIBILITY: Australian citizens or permanent residents based in Australia\; 
 tertiary students including PhD candidates are ineligible\, as are past Sy
 napse recipients within 10 years\; the fee covers one artist\, artist grou
 ps are ineligible. ASSESSMENT: by an independent art-science panel\, with 
 notification in late November 2026. DEADLINE: 14 October 2026 at 3 pm ACDT
 . Residency takes place between February and October 2027.\n\nOrganisation
 : Australian Network for Art and Technology (ANAT)\nLocation: An Australia
 n research organisation chosen by the artist (onsite/offsite mix). Open to
  Australian citizens or permanent residents based in Australia.\nAward: To
 tal artist fee of AUD 19\,250 ex GST plus 12% superannuation\, plus up to 
 AUD 3\,500 toward other project expenses. No application fee.\nDuration: 1
 6 weeks full-time (or part-time equivalent)\, between February and October
  2027.\n\nMore: https://www.anat.org.au/program/2027-synapse-call/?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.anat.org.au/program/2027-synapse-call/?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:An Australian research organisation chosen by the artist (onsite/o
 ffsite mix). Open to Australian citizens or permanent residents based in A
 ustralia.
END:VEVENT
