DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: Art Explora x Cité internationale des arts Residency\, 7
 th Call (Paris)
DESCRIPTION:The 7th call of the Art Explora residency programme at the Cit
 é internationale des arts opened 21 September 2026. The programme support
 s projects exploring the crossovers of art with science\, technology and e
 cology\, which makes it one of the stronger art-science fits in Europe. Re
 sidents receive a furnished live-work studio of around 50 m2 in Paris\, EU
 R 1\,000 per month living stipend\, up to EUR 3\,000 production budget\, r
 ound-trip travel and mentoring\, with residencies of 3 or 6 months for sol
 o artists and 3 months for duos of an artist with a researcher\, curator o
 r writer. Open to visual\, performing and digital artists of all nationali
 ties and ages with at least 5 years of professional experience and an inte
 rnational exhibition record. Programme details at artexplora.org. TO APPLY
 : submit via the Art Explora application platform. DEADLINE: 30 October 20
 26\, 11:59 PM Paris time.\n\nOrganisation: Art Explora Foundation and Cit
 é internationale des arts\nLocation: Paris\, France. Open worldwide to ar
 tists with at least 5 years of professional practice.\nAward: EUR 1\,000 p
 er month living stipend plus up to EUR 3\,000 production grant\, a furnish
 ed live-work studio of around 50 m2 at the Cité internationale des arts\,
  round-trip travel to Paris and curatorial mentoring. No application fee.\
 nDuration: 3- or 6-month residencies during 2027\; 3 months for duos (arti
 st plus researcher\, curator or writer).\n\nMore: https://artexplora.plate
 formecandidature.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=ref
 erral
URL:https://artexplora.plateformecandidature.com/?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Paris\, France. Open worldwide to artists with at least 5 years of
  professional practice.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:eyebeam-agency-virtual-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115744Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261011
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261012
SUMMARY:Deadline: Eyebeam AGENCY Virtual Residency\, Fall 2026 (US-based ar
 tists)
DESCRIPTION:Eyebeam's 2026-27 program year runs under the theme AGENCY: pre
 serving human agency as AI systems increasingly act\, decide and carry out
  tasks on our behalf\, asserting agency in imagining and building the soci
 eties we inhabit\, and rethinking agency as collective\, relational\, enta
 ngled and more-than-human. The Virtual Residency (Fall/Winter) supports US
 -based artists working outside New York City with time\, community and str
 ucture to develop new work around the theme\; it is well-suited to early-s
 tage projects where shared research\, discussion groups and feedback on na
 scent ideas would advance concept development and prototyping. Projects mi
 ght engage AI directly but do not have to\; Eyebeam welcomes critical and 
 creative approaches to power\, autonomy\, technological systems\, collecti
 ve action\, human and nonhuman relationships\, and the structures through 
 which agency is exercised\, including reimagining AI systems through colle
 ctive governance\, repair\, rehearsal or mischief\, and repurposing AI tow
 ard tools for the public good. STRUCTURE: six artists\, 12 weeks\, minimum
  3-4 hours per week\, with weekly cohort sessions\, independent project de
 velopment\, work-in-progress shares with peers and guest critics\, a closi
 ng virtual process presentation\, and a contribution to an end-of-year pub
 lication. ELIGIBILITY: individuals only (no collectives this cycle)\; not 
 enrolled in a full-time degree program\; not committed to another residenc
 y during the term\; US-based outside NYC for the full term. TIMELINE: dead
 line Sunday 11 October 2026\, 11:59 PM ET (no late applications)\; intervi
 ews 26-28 October\; notifications 29 October\; residency 4 November 2026 t
 o 12 February 2027. Info session Monday 28 September 2026\, 1 PM ET. Apply
  via Submittable\, free.\n\nOrganisation: Eyebeam\nLocation: Online. Appli
 cants must be based in the United States\, OUTSIDE New York City\, and rem
 ain US-based for the full residency term (4 November 2026 to 12 February 2
 027).\nAward: USD 2\,000 stipend for each of six selected artists\, plus w
 eekly residency programming\, mentorship with Eyebeam alumni and visiting 
 professionals\, technical consultation\, and access to tools and expertise
  through Eyebeam's network. No application fee (via Submittable).\nDuratio
 n: 12 weeks\, 4 November 2026 to 12 February 2027\; minimum commitment 3-4
  hours per week.\n\nMore: https://eyebeam.org/articles/agency-virtual-resi
 dency?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://eyebeam.org/articles/agency-virtual-residency?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online. Applicants must be based in the United States\, OUTSIDE Ne
 w York City\, and remain US-based for the full residency term (4 November 
 2026 to 12 February 2027).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:eyebeam-agency-nyc-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115744Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:Deadline: Eyebeam AGENCY NYC Residency\, Spring 2027
DESCRIPTION:The NYC track of Eyebeam's AGENCY residency cycle supports New 
 York City-based artists exploring questions of agency at a moment when AI 
 systems increasingly act\, decide and carry out tasks on our behalf: how t
 o preserve human agency as these systems shape human behavior\, how to ass
 ert agency in imagining and building the societies we inhabit\, and what a
 gency becomes when understood as collective\, relational\, entangled and m
 ore-than-human. Projects might engage AI directly but do not have to\; cri
 tical and creative approaches to power\, autonomy\, technological systems\
 , collective action\, human and nonhuman relationships\, and the social an
 d material structures of agency are all welcome\, including reimagining AI
  through collective governance\, repair\, rehearsal or mischief\, and repu
 rposing AI systems toward new tools\, methods and models for the public go
 od. Residents receive a USD 5\,000 stipend\, mentorship\, and access to to
 ols and technical expertise through Eyebeam's network. ELIGIBILITY: indivi
 duals only (no collectives this cycle)\; not enrolled in a full-time degre
 e program\; not committed to another residency during the term\; must live
  in New York City within the five boroughs and be able to work on site at 
 Eyebeam at least one day a week for the full term. TIMELINE: deadline Sund
 ay 15 November 2026\, 11:59 PM ET\; interviews 7-10 December\; notificatio
 ns 14 December\; residency 15 March to 11 June 2027. Info session Monday 1
 9 October 2026\, 1 PM ET. Apply via Submittable\, free.\n\nOrganisation: E
 yebeam\nLocation: New York City\, USA. Applicants must live within the fiv
 e boroughs and be able to work on site at Eyebeam at least one day a week 
 for the full residency term (15 March to 11 June 2027).\nAward: USD 5\,000
  stipend per selected artist\, plus mentorship and access to tools and tec
 hnical expertise through Eyebeam's network. No application fee (via Submit
 table).\nDuration: 15 March to 11 June 2027\; on site at Eyebeam at least 
 one day per week.\n\nMore: https://eyebeam.org/articles/agency-nyc-residen
 cy?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://eyebeam.org/articles/agency-nyc-residency?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:New York City\, USA. Applicants must live within the five boroughs
  and be able to work on site at Eyebeam at least one day a week for the fu
 ll residency term (15 March to 11 June 2027).
END:VEVENT
