DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: SAM Residencies Open Call: Cycle 4 (2027/2028) at Singapo
 re Art Museum
DESCRIPTION:The Singapore Art Museum's SAM Residencies programme\, hosted i
 n post-industrial warehouse spaces at Tanjong Pagar Distripark\, opens its
  fourth cycle for residencies between June 2027 and December 2028. Three t
 racks are available: Artist Residency (new artistic research\, experimenta
 tion and modes of making)\, Community & Education Residency (practice at t
 he intersection of art\, education and community engagement)\, and Curator
 ial & Research Residency (new approaches to exhibition making and curatori
 al practice). SUPPORT: a monthly stipend of SGD 1\,500 and a shared studio
  or co-working space for all residents\; international residents also get 
 a return economy flight\, housing arrangement and visa assistance\, while 
 Singapore-based residents get an additional monthly local allowance of SGD
  250. Residents lead at least two public presentations or activations\, su
 ch as Residency Thursdays\, Open Studios or an In Conversation showcase. E
 LIGIBILITY: open globally to artists\, curators\, educators\, researchers 
 and creative practitioners\; individuals\, duos and collectives from all m
 ediums and disciplines\; applicants must be over 21. International applica
 nts may apply for one to three months\, Singapore-based applicants for up 
 to six months. HOW TO APPLY: via the SurveyMonkey Apply portal with a CV\,
  portfolio\, statement of interest (500-1\,000 words) and a recommendation
  letter submitted by the recommender. No application fee. Queries to resid
 encies@singaporeartmuseum.sg. DEADLINE: 30 September 2026 at 11:59 PM (GMT
 +8).\n\nOrganisation: Singapore Art Museum\nLocation: Tanjong Pagar Distri
 park\, Singapore. Open to artists\, curators\, educators\, researchers and
  creative practitioners from across the globe\; individuals\, duos and col
 lectives welcome.\nAward: Monthly stipend of SGD 1\,500 plus a shared stud
 io or co-working space for all residents. International residents also rec
 eive a return economy flight\, housing arrangement and visa assistance\; S
 ingapore-based residents receive an additional monthly local allowance of 
 SGD 250. No application fee.\nDuration: Residency period June 2027 to Dece
 mber 2028\; international applicants may apply for one to three months\, S
 ingapore-based applicants for up to six months\n\nMore: https://www.singap
 oreartmuseum.sg/residencies/announcements/open-call-cycle-4?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.singaporeartmuseum.sg/residencies/announcements/open-call-c
 ycle-4?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Tanjong Pagar Distripark\, Singapore. Open to artists\, curators\,
  educators\, researchers and creative practitioners from across the globe\
 ; individuals\, duos and collectives welcome.
END:VEVENT
