UID:hiap-learning-materials-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115744Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261026
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261027
SUMMARY:Deadline: HIAP: Learning Materials International Artist Residency 2
 027 (Suomenlinna\, Helsinki)
DESCRIPTION:HIAP's Learning Materials international residency hosts artists
  at HIAP Suomenlinna\, the island fortress off Helsinki\, for 90 days in S
 pring 2027 (12 April to 11 July) or Autumn 2027 (16 August to 14 November)
 . The call suits artists with established material-based practices\, socia
 lly engaged practitioners and researchers exploring ecology and materials\
 ; the residency is research-focused with no required output. DISCIPLINES: 
 digital\, visual arts\, interdisciplinary and research practices. WHAT YOU
  GET: a working grant of EUR 1\,350 per month (EUR 4\,050 in total) via Ko
 ne Foundation\, a material budget up to EUR 750\, an access budget up to E
 UR 1\,000\, one return trip from the artist's home with slow travel encour
 aged and help with travel arrangements\, plus accommodation and workspace.
  ELIGIBILITY: international artists and arts practitioners living and work
 ing outside Finland. Collectives may apply\, but the working grant can be 
 paid to one individual only and there are no extra residency fees or addit
 ional travel budget. APPLICATION: free\, via the online form on the HIAP w
 ebsite. DEADLINE: 26 October 2026\, 15:00 UTC.\n\nOrganisation: HIAP (Hels
 inki International Artist Programme)\, with Kone Foundation\nLocation: HIA
 P Suomenlinna\, Helsinki\, Finland. Open to artists living and working out
 side Finland.\nAward: Working grant of EUR 1\,350 per month (EUR 4\,050 to
 tal for 90 days) via Kone Foundation\, material budget up to EUR 750\, acc
 ess budget up to EUR 1\,000\, one return trip covered (slow travel encoura
 ged)\, plus accommodation and workspace. For collectives\, the working gra
 nt can be paid to one individual only and there is no additional travel bu
 dget.\nDuration: 90 days: Spring 2027 (12 April to 11 July) or Autumn 2027
  (16 August to 14 November).\n\nMore: https://www.hiap.fi/learning-materia
 ls-international-residency-application-form-2027/?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.hiap.fi/learning-materials-international-residency-applicat
 ion-form-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:HIAP Suomenlinna\, Helsinki\, Finland. Open to artists living and 
 working outside Finland.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:witte-rook-izolyatsia-digital-explorers-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261031T115744Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:Deadline: Witte Rook x IZOLYATSIA: Digital Explorers (Across Border
 s) Online Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:Witte Rook (Breda) and the Ukrainian platform IZOLYATSIA run Di
 gital Explorers (Across Borders)\, a fully online residency program explor
 ing the artist-in-residence of the future through cross-border collaborati
 on. Each of three phases pairs one artist from the Netherlands with one fr
 om Ukraine\, working together for about three months on the common.garden 
 platform. WHAT YOU GET: EUR 1\,800 fee plus EUR 1\,000 material budget per
  artist (both excluding VAT)\, expert discussions\, technical support\, a 
 physical and online exhibition (final exhibitions planned for spring 2028)
  and a published article about the creative process. ELIGIBILITY: artists 
 and makers working in digital culture and interested in new technology who
  live and work in the Netherlands or Ukraine\; proficiency in English requ
 ired. APPLICATION: in English via the IZOLYATSIA platform\; motivation let
 ter (max 1\,000 words)\, CV (max 3 A4 pages) and portfolio (max 10 A4 page
 s\, 20 MB)\; applicants indicate a first and second priority phase. PHASES
 : 'Form' (January to March 2027)\, 'Content' (May to July 2027)\, 'Analysi
 s' (September to December 2027). DEADLINE: 15 November 2026\, 23:59 CET.\n
 \nOrganisation: Witte Rook and IZOLYATSIA\nLocation: Online\, on the commo
 n.garden platform. Open to artists living and working in the Netherlands o
 r Ukraine. Organizers based in Breda (NL) and Ukraine.\nAward: EUR 1\,800 
 artist fee (excluding VAT) plus EUR 1\,000 material budget (excluding VAT)
  per artist. Six artists selected in total (three Dutch-Ukrainian pairs). 
 No application fee.\nDuration: Approximately three months per phase: Phase
  1 'Form' (January to March 2027)\, Phase 2 'Content' (May to July 2027)\,
  Phase 3 'Analysis' (September to December 2027).\n\nMore: https://wittero
 ok.nl/agenda/open-call-digital-explorers/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://witterook.nl/agenda/open-call-digital-explorers/?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online\, on the common.garden platform. Open to artists living and
  working in the Netherlands or Ukraine. Organizers based in Breda (NL) and
  Ukraine.
END:VEVENT
