UID:tate-delfina-brooks-international-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.git
 hub.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115744Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Tate x Delfina Foundation: Brooks International Fellowshi
 p Programme 2027 (London)
DESCRIPTION:Now in its thirteenth year\, the Brooks International Fellowshi
 p Programme places international researchers within Tate Britain's Curator
 ial Division for six months\, with accommodation and a parallel residency 
 programme at Delfina Foundation. TWO FELLOWSHIPS IN 2027: Leonora Carringt
 on: Art and the Theatre of Life\, researching the British-Mexican artist's
  engagement with theatre and performance (knowledge of Mexican social-poli
 tical context and performance history particularly useful)\; and Artist Su
 pported Studios\, research and development for the 2028 Tate Britain Commi
 ssion focused on supported studios working with disabled and neurodivergen
 t artists. WHAT YOU GET: return economy flight\, UK airport transfers\, vi
 sa fee reimbursement and visa support\, GBP 40 per day living allowance\, 
 London transport pass\, a single bedroom at Delfina Foundation\, travel to
  other Tate sites and UK/European institutions\, plus Delfina's programme 
 of visits\, presentations and professional development\; the Carrington fe
 llowship adds a research resource allowance. ELIGIBILITY: international re
 searchers based outside the UK. APPLICATION: not online\; download the Wor
 d application form for your chosen fellowship from Tate's job portal and e
 mail it to international.fellowships@tate.org.uk (alternative formats such
  as video or audio are described in the Open Call PDF). DEADLINE: 21 Octob
 er 2026\, 17:00 GMT\; late applications not accepted.\n\nOrganisation: Tat
 e and Delfina Foundation\nLocation: Tate Britain Curatorial Division\, Lon
 don\, UK\, with accommodation and complementary activities at Delfina Foun
 dation. Open to international researchers based outside the UK.\nAward: No
 n-salaried but fully supported: return economy-class flight\, UK airport t
 ransfers\, visa fee reimbursement and visa support via Delfina Foundation\
 , a living allowance bursary of GBP 40 per day\, a London Underground and 
 bus travel pass\, a single bedroom at Delfina Foundation with shared facil
 ities\, and travel to other Tate galleries and UK/European cultural instit
 utions. The Leonora Carrington fellowship adds a research resource allowan
 ce. No application fee.\nDuration: Six months\, 5 April to 17 September 20
 27.\n\nMore: https://www.delfinafoundation.com/open-calls/current/open-cal
 l-with-tate-for-brooks-international-fellowship-programme-2027/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.delfinafoundation.com/open-calls/current/open-call-with-tat
 e-for-brooks-international-fellowship-programme-2027/?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Tate Britain Curatorial Division\, London\, UK\, with accommodatio
 n and complementary activities at Delfina Foundation. Open to internationa
 l researchers based outside the UK.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:yao-residency-02-taiwan-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115744Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Deadline: YAO Residency #02 (Taiwan): Research Residency 2027 and E
 xhibition 2028
DESCRIPTION:YAO Residency #02 centres on the translation between culture an
 d material: through living\, research and exchange in Taiwan\, artists eng
 age with different cultural contexts\, local ways of living\, materials an
 d craft practices\, with emphasis on process rather than finished works. O
 NE artist/practitioner is selected for a two-phase program. PHASE ONE (res
 earch residency\, 21 August to 21 November 2027): field research\, materia
 l exploration and local engagement\, closing with an Open Studio (27 Octob
 er to 16 November 2027) presenting research in progress. PHASE TWO (2028):
  the artist returns to Taiwan for a formal exhibition or other public pres
 entation at YAO\, expected to run at least six weeks. WHAT YOU GET: per ph
 ase\, travel support (international applicants up to NTD 20\,000 round-tri
 p against receipts)\, a living stipend of NTD 10\,000 and accommodation\; 
 Phase One adds a production budget of up to NTD 20\,000\, an Open Studio v
 enue and help connecting with craftspeople\, communities and cultural prac
 titioners\; Phase Two adds the exhibition venue\, installation assistance 
 and documentation\; both phases include text editing\, translation and pro
 motional support. ELIGIBILITY: artists\, makers\, researchers and interdis
 ciplinary practitioners aged 18 or over with an ongoing creative practice\
 , any nationality\; suited to self-directed researchers who transform rese
 arch into artistic practice. APPLICATION: via Google Form as a single PDF 
 with CV\, artist statement\, portfolio and a residency proposal covering m
 ethodology\, research themes\, areas of Taiwan engagement (materials\, cra
 fts\, environments\, cultural contexts)\, planned activities and possible 
 creative directions\; in Mandarin or English. FEE: NTD 300 (Taiwan-based\,
  bank transfer) or USD 10 (international\, PayPal)\, non-refundable\; uplo
 ad proof of payment. TIMELINE: interview invitations 10 January 2027\, onl
 ine interviews 16 January\, selection announced 29 January 2027. DEADLINE:
  31 December 2026.\n\nOrganisation: YAO Residency Program (Yao Zuo Zhu Cun
  Ji Hua)\nLocation: Taiwan. Open worldwide to applicants aged 18 and above
 \, regardless of nationality\; international artists arrange their own ent
 ry and visa (YAO can provide an invitation letter).\nAward: Research Resid
 ency 2027: travel support (international applicants reimbursed up to NTD 2
 0\,000 for one round-trip to Taiwan against receipts)\, production budget 
 up to NTD 20\,000\, living stipend of NTD 10\,000\, accommodation\, Open S
 tudio venue\, local connections\, and documentation\, text editing\, trans
 lation and promotional support. Exhibition Phase 2028: travel support up t
 o NTD 20\,000 again\, a further NTD 10\,000 living stipend\, accommodation
 \, exhibition venue at YAO\, installation and de-installation assistance\,
  and exhibition documentation. Application fee: NTD 300 for Taiwan-based a
 pplicants (bank transfer) or USD 10 for international applicants (PayPal)\
 , non-refundable.\nDuration: Two phases: research residency 21 August to 2
 1 November 2027 with Open Studio 27 October to 16 November 2027\, then a f
 ormal exhibition at YAO in 2028 (expected to run at least six weeks\, date
 s agreed with the artist). The selected artist commits to both phases.\n\n
 More: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfQ5-RBrfPckf4O9A5LeDrAzbFl
 XHzBkYrpPyTiy3HeKc8BkQ/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
 medium=referral
URL:https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfQ5-RBrfPckf4O9A5LeDrAzbFlXHz
 BkYrpPyTiy3HeKc8BkQ/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Taiwan. Open worldwide to applicants aged 18 and above\, regardles
 s of nationality\; international artists arrange their own entry and visa 
 (YAO can provide an invitation letter).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jan-van-eyck-residency-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115744Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Deadline: Jan van Eyck Academie Residency 2028 (Maastricht\, 11 mon
 ths)
DESCRIPTION:The Jan van Eyck Academie's general open call for its 2028 resi
 dency year: 30 to 32 artists\, curators\, designers\, writers\, architects
  and other artistic researchers spend 11 months (15 January to 15 December
  2028) in Maastricht\, across material-based and research-driven practices
 \, with access to the academy's labs and community. Individuals\, duos\, c
 ollectives and candidates with children can apply\; duos and collectives s
 ubmit one application and pay one fee. SUPPORT: monthly stipend of EUR 1\,
 500 (EUR 2\,000 with children\; duos EUR 1\,500 each or EUR 2\,500 combine
 d for life partners\; collectives up to EUR 4\,500 combined)\, with rent i
 ncluding service costs deducted\; EUR 2\,000 annual working budget\; newly
  built furnished private studio apartments (families get a spacious privat
 e apartment\; collectives up to three studio apartments\, possibly on rota
 tion). ELIGIBILITY: no nationality or age restriction\; sufficient English
  required (Dutch and English are the working languages)\; full-time alumni
  of the Rijksakademie or De Ateliers are not eligible\; the academy is not
  an educational institute and provides no degrees or ECTS. FEES: applicati
 on fee EUR 65 excl. VAT (EUR 78.65 incl. VAT)\, waived for applicants from
  and living in OECD DAC-list ODA recipient countries\; enrolment fee EUR 2
 \,750 excl. VAT for accepted participants. APPLY via the Dapple platform w
 ith an artist statement (250 words)\, motivation (500 words) and project p
 roposal (500 words) in English (or one video/audio/link covering all three
 )\, plus one PDF (max 10 MB) with recent work from the last five years (ma
 x 25 pages) and a CV (max 2 pages)\; applications cannot be changed after 
 submission. TIMELINE: call opened 5 October 2026\; selection outcome mid-M
 ay 2027. DEADLINE: 1 December 2026\, 23:59 CET.\n\nOrganisation: Jan van E
 yck Academie\nLocation: Maastricht\, Netherlands. Open worldwide\; partici
 pants must settle in Maastricht and register with the municipality (the ac
 ademy applies for visas where relevant).\nAward: Monthly stipend of EUR 1\
 ,500 (EUR 2\,000 for participants with children\; EUR 1\,500 per duo membe
 r or EUR 2\,500 combined for life partners\; collectives up to EUR 4\,500 
 combined\, max three stipends)\, with rent including service costs deducte
 d from the stipend. Plus a EUR 2\,000 annual working budget and a newly bu
 ilt\, furnished private studio apartment. Application fee EUR 65 excl. VAT
  (EUR 78.65 incl. VAT)\, waived for applicants from and living in OECD DAC
 -list countries\; enrolment fee for accepted participants EUR 2\,750 excl.
  VAT.\nDuration: 11 months\, 15 January to 15 December 2028\; 30 to 32 pos
 itions\; selection outcome mid-May 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.janvaneyck.n
 l/calendar/apply-now-jve-residency-2028?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.janvaneyck.nl/calendar/apply-now-jve-residency-2028?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Maastricht\, Netherlands. Open worldwide\; participants must settl
 e in Maastricht and register with the municipality (the academy applies fo
 r visas where relevant).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cifnl-videotage-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115744Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative Industries Fund NL: Residency Videotage 2027 (Ho
 ng Kong)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL offers one residency at Videota
 ge\, the Hong Kong media art institute (est. 1986) known for critical work
  on XR\, AI\, blockchain and video games. The 2027 edition takes the techn
 ological 'black box' phenomenon as its starting point: deep neural network
 s now shape social media\, healthcare\, finance\, governance and justice w
 hile their inner workings remain hard to grasp\, and the resident is invit
 ed to explore this through media art in Hong Kong's urban context. WHO: an
  individual designer\, maker or observer within digital culture\, establis
 hed in the Netherlands or the Caribbean parts of the Kingdom\, registered 
 with the KvK (or another Kingdom business register)\, with at least four y
 ears of professional practice. NOT for duos\, collectives\, or recipients 
 of CIFNL Talent Development\, Self-taught Designer or Emerging Design Prac
 tices ABCSSS grants during the work period (winning this excludes applying
  to those schemes in 2027). SUPPORT: EUR 5\,000 (two months) or EUR 6\,500
  (three months) for travel\, insurance\, living costs\, time and materials
 \; housing\, workspace\, curatorial guidance and production costs are paid
  directly to Videotage\; accommodation arranged by Videotage\; access to e
 quipment and the Videotage Media Art Collection archive. SELECTION: tender
 -style ranking by an external advisory committee on artistic quality\, pro
 ject quality and motivation\; the top five proposals go to Videotage\, whi
 ch co-decides\; decision within eight weeks of closing. APPLY via the Fund
 's application platform (aanvragen.stimuleringsfonds.nl)\, round 'Open Cal
 l Residencies 2027'\, preferably in English: work plan (max 4 A4 / 4 MB PD
 F)\, brief CV (max 2 A4)\, portfolio (max 8 A4 / 8 MB)\, certified KvK ext
 ract under one year old\, and a representative JPG image. NOTE: account ac
 tivation on the platform takes one working day\, so register early. DEADLI
 NE: 21 October 2026\, 16:00 CEST.\n\nOrganisation: Creative Industries Fun
 d NL (Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie)\, with Videotage\nLocation: H
 ong Kong (Videotage premises). Only for applicants established in the Neth
 erlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarte
 n and registered with a Kingdom of the Netherlands business register (KvK)
 .\nAward: One residency grant: EUR 5\,000 for a two-month work period or E
 UR 6\,500 for three months\, covering travel\, insurance\, living expenses
 \, compensation for time invested\, and material and transport costs. Hous
 ing\, work space\, Videotage guidance and production costs are paid by the
  Fund directly to Videotage on top of the grant\; accommodation is arrange
 d by Videotage. No application fee.\nDuration: 23 March to 18 May 2027 (tw
 o months) or 23 March to 15 June 2027 (three months)\; state your preferre
 d period. Research period plus a concluding public presentation event for 
 Videotage's Hong Kong network.\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/e
 n/grants/open-call-videotage?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-videotage?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hong Kong (Videotage premises). Only for applicants established in
  the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Si
 nt Maarten and registered with a Kingdom of the Netherlands business regis
 ter (KvK).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mensch-maschine-visit-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261031T115744Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mensch Maschine VISIT Residency Fellowship 2027: Energy G
 hosts (E-WERK Luckenwalde / Akademie der Künste)
DESCRIPTION:The Mensch Maschine VISIT Residency Program is an annual fellow
 ship offering four fully funded fellowships to artists from around the wor
 ld\, run by the JUNGE AKADEMIE of the Akademie der Künste (Berlin) with V
 ISIT\, the artist-in-residence programme of the E.ON Foundation\, E-WERK L
 uckenwalde and Ujazdowski Castle Centre for Contemporary Art (Warsaw). The
  2027 edition particularly encourages projects at the intersection of art\
 , energy and ecology exploring the theme ENERGY GHOSTS: the unseen dimensi
 ons of energy approached through mythology\, cosmology or speculative fict
 ion\, the invisible infrastructures\, histories and residues that haunt co
 ntemporary life\, and energy as an ecological\, political or spiritual for
 ce. Proposals are welcome from visual art\, performance\, film\, installat
 ion\, sound\, writing and new media. WHAT YOU GET: EUR 20\,000 per fellow 
 for artist fees and production costs of a new project (research and develo
 pment\, travel\, material and presentation costs)\; three fellows receive 
 studio space and accommodation at E-WERK Luckenwalde (a former power stati
 on about 40 minutes south of Berlin)\, one is accommodated by the Akademie
  der Künste in Berlin. The three-month residency runs roughly September t
 o November 2027 with on-site presence of at least 75% required\, a retreat
  at Ujazdowski Castle in Warsaw in September 2027\, events across the thre
 e venues\, and a closing symposium in October 2027 at the Akademie der Kü
 nste where fellows show work in progress alongside the 2026 cohort. JURY: 
 Nolan Oswald Dennis\; Chus Martinez (Institute Art Gender Nature\, TBA21)\
 ; Sarah Johanna Theurer (Fondation Beyeler)\; Anh-Linh Ngo (Akademie der K
 ünste)\; and Tiara Roxanne. APPLICATION: via the VISIT portal at visit-en
 ergy.com/bewerben. DEADLINE: 1 December 2026\, 23:59 CET.\n\nOrganisation:
  JUNGE AKADEMIE of the Akademie der Künste\, VISIT (E.ON Foundation)\, E-
 WERK Luckenwalde and Ujazdowski Castle Centre for Contemporary Art\nLocati
 on: E-WERK Luckenwalde\, Brandenburg\, Germany (3 fellows) and Akademie de
 r Künste\, Berlin (1 fellow)\, with a retreat at Ujazdowski Castle CCA in
  Warsaw\, Poland. Open to artists worldwide.\nAward: Four fully funded fel
 lowships of EUR 20\,000 each\, intended for artist fees and production cos
 ts of a new project (research and development\, travel\, materials and pre
 sentation costs)\, plus studio space and accommodation for the three-month
  residency.\nDuration: Three months\, roughly September to November 2027 (
 the AdK notice gives mid-August to mid-November)\; fellows must live and w
 ork on site at least 75% of the time.\n\nMore: https://adk.de/news/2026/10
 /open-call-mensch-maschine-stipendium?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://adk.de/news/2026/10/open-call-mensch-maschine-stipendium?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:E-WERK Luckenwalde\, Brandenburg\, Germany (3 fellows) and Akademi
 e der Künste\, Berlin (1 fellow)\, with a retreat at Ujazdowski Castle CC
 A in Warsaw\, Poland. Open to artists worldwide.
